[test-suite name=session
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/session (spec/02-inprogress/xap/stdlib_session.md §10).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/session'] (the
   resolver MUST be quoted) and composes the shipped cx-stdlib/crypto (token
   verify), cx-stdlib/http ([request]/[header] shapes), cx-stdlib/time (the
   pinned `now`), and cx-stdlib/strings (cookie-value concat). The LAST
   expression is the rendered result.

   HERMETIC GOLDEN TOKEN (reused from crypto-071): an RS256 JWT signed by a
   local test IdP, verified against a LITERAL in-memory JWKS (kid rsa-1) — so
   every fixture needs NO `net` (the air-gapped posture, §5). The token's
   verified claims are iss="https://idp.example", sub="user-1", aud="my-api",
   exp=1700003600, nbf=1699999990. The pinned clock is
   [$time:datetime 2023 11 14 22 13 20] (= Unix 1700000000), inside the
   token's validity window — identical to crypto-071..075.

   The golden token carries NO `tid` claim, so the attach config maps the
   tenant from the `aud` claim (tenant-claim: "aud" → tenant "my-api") and the
   principal from `sub` (the default → "user-1"). This exercises the §2.3
   claim-mapping with the existing golden material — no new key minting.

   DETERMINISM: the opaque session id and the CSRF synchronizer token are
   CSPRNG (≥128-bit, §2.8/§2.9) — fresh per attach. They are NEVER asserted by
   literal value (exactly like the crypto random fixtures). Instead the
   fixtures pin STRUCTURE: the session-id prefix ("s-"), the round-trip
   (from-cookie resolves the same [session]; csrf-verify passes with the
   read-back token), and the stable attributes (principal/tenant binding,
   state, client `via` markers, cookie flags).

   Id ranges:
     001-006  attach + the (principal,tenant) binding + accessors + map-claims
     007-010  of/by-id/by-client resolution + the absence channel
     011-015  mirrored attach + survives-client-death + detach idempotent + touch
     016-024  cookie transport: attach-cookie + set-cookie flags + from-cookie
              round-trip + rotate + clear-cookie
     025-031  CSRF: token read + verify pass/missing/mismatch + Bearer-exempt
     032-045  negatives: 4801/4802/4803/4804/4805/4806/4807/4810/4811
#]]

 [case id=session-001-attach-binds-principal-tenant level=core gate=enforced
  [tags session attach binding]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/session']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/crypto']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $s [$session:attach [request scheme="https" [headers [header name="Authorization" value="Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6InJzYS0xIiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0.eyJpc3MiOiJodHRwczovL2lkcC5leGFtcGxlIiwic3ViIjoidXNlci0xIiwiYXVkIjoibXktYXBpIiwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMDAzNjAwLCJuYmYiOjE2OTk5OTk5OTAsImlhdCI6MTY5OTk5OTk5MH0.e4bn1A_a5Q0_4IZxKWipmmrUCCdmNkiTUs071mBMtMVXb68RGPtV2FTR1nRWvM3Zw2XTMuBsk_Y1HPinat_2JQkm3s90lltrErpYOky6Nwm6ha57BxQ0Sg5kWxuQF5KhWUqHzePIVDTfkr0WeN591nDTDn6VuajLaHn2pjXBsaJ0reT6mh6v40UQcBW-yy-XOfrsMeGVj_qZd1UmlE81XN957rjPENcPpH2E1SHfVhu3fQP3QZapxtdMADgWmryw_z5O2lDIIWb7miT0siXRCDjVEhDzKH6Hsf1aUPcYx9x44o1B5OBpX6z1uM1SP0qaOZu6x26H0AbHj84nIISE1A"]]] {jwks: [$crypto:jwks-parse "{\"keys\":[{\"kid\":\"rsa-1\",\"kty\":\"RSA\",\"alg\":\"RS256\",\"n\":\"jdwwBcaMZQLoSNYGNEm3l03HIQqpRIv0eqLUNUCkyv7ysVw4i6vZgdYxcdU0D3kSvUCIjH-icqk4PCDx5AwkeNp55Nqt6wKXDv9TH5pr-Wc3BWmZ1sEOEwyN8QlI8_5EpY3i1w5tysDdeFuiR7BOjpkD49RZzF0YajmocsB4_jXoZcldVNCOChXAbEfOw-BtjFJRN0N3EksymF4azkey8Q3rX07sXkRHavRfAOnowH119RL1V-Xmk_DUX8wSR-2zdlp8FxitJWPgbMmnszsTgEQrThTwsuMrndqzJ_nQ7HTnuK2LXEFmFwXw9NADspq2ZnQmZiN7CXnEYG8WCApzxw\",\"e\":\"AQAB\"}]}"] tenant-claim: "aud" now: [$time:datetime 2023 11 14 22 13 20]}]] [$session:principal $s]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[principal id=user-1 [tenant id=my-api]]
#]]
 ]

